d, then picks the keyboard map’s nearest mapped note number. With the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"configuration — "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/KeyboardMap\/a440"},{"type":"text","text":", 12-tone equal temperament, and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchStandard\/a440"},{"type":"text","text":" —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this matches the usual piano key assignments, so B♯3 and C4 both convert to 60, and C♭4 to 59."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because conversion goes through frequency, a pitch standard that differs from the keyboard"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"map’s reference transposes the result rather than being an error. For example, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/PitchStandard\/a415"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/KeyboardMap\/a440"},{"type":"text","text":", A4 converts to 68, the key that sounds closest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to 415 Hz. In tuning systems other than 12-tone equal temperament, a pitch may convert to a key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"other than the one its spelling suggests: in quarter-comma meantone, B𝄪3 sounds about 45 cents"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"above C4 — nearer C4 than C♯4 — so it converts to 60, not 61."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/standardtokeyboardpitchconverter"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning"]]},"identifier":{"interf